3.3V SRAM and I/O test chip
------------------------
This chip uses a standard wafer.spice 1/2 size frame.
However, to test the 3.3V libraries, the following
changes are made:

(1) Pads are changed to the equivalent ocd_io pad library
    cells, except that the 24um drive pads are replaced
    with standard selectable drive pads.

(2) Every other pair of DVDD/DVSS pads are replaced with
    VDD/VSS pads (3.3V).

(3) The analog pads are not used

(4) The padframe uses a local loopback scheme to provide
    a fixed programming to each bidirectional pad to make
    it either input or output.

(5) Pad assignments are as follows, starting at the lower
    left hand corner and working counter-clockwise:

    Bottom row:
     1 (input only) CLK
     2 (input only) rst_n	(PoR enable)
     3 GWEN
     4 POR output (porb---low during reset)
     5 VSS
     6 VDD
     7 A7	(except for 64 byte SRAM)
     8 A6	(except for 64 byte SRAM)
     9 A5
    10 A4
    11 A3
    12 A2
    13 A1
    14 A0
    15 D7
    16 D6
    17 D5
    18 D4
    19 DVSS
    20 DVDD
    21 D3
    22 D2
    23 D1
    24 D0

   Right side
    25 VSS
    26 VDD
    27 CEN (1024 byte SRAM)
    28 CEN (512 byte SRAM)
    29 CEN (256 byte SRAM)
    30 CEN (64 byte SRAM)
    31 WEN7
    32 WEN6
    33 WEN5
    34 WEN4
    35 DVSS
    36 DVDD

   Top side
    37 WEN3
    38 WEN2
    39 WEN1
    40 WEN0
    41 VDD
    42 VSS
    43 Q7 (1024/512 byte)
    44 Q6 (1024/512 byte)
    45 Q5 (1024/512 byte)
    46 Q4 (1024/512 byte)
    47 Q3 (1024/512 byte)
    48 Q2 (1024/512 byte)
    49 Q1 (1024/512 byte)
    50 Q0 (1024/512 byte)
    51 Q7 (256/64 byte)
    52 Q6 (256/64 byte)
    53 Q5 (256/64 byte)
    54 Q4 (256/64 byte)
    55 DVDD
    56 DVSS
    57 Q3 (256/64 byte)
    58 Q2 (256/64 byte)
    59 Q1 (256/64 byte)
    60 Q0 (256/64 byte)

   Left side
    61 VDD
    62 VSS
    63 (analog, unused)
    64 (analog, unused)
    65 (analog, unused)
    66 (analog, unused)
    67 (input only) output select:  1024 byte or 512 byte
    68 (input only) A9 (1024 byte SRAM only)
    69 (input only) output select:  256 byte or 64 byte
    70 (input only) A8 (512 and 1024 byte SRAMs only)
    71 DVDD
    72 DVSS

----------------------------------------------------
Build procedure:
----------------------------------------------------

    cd magic
    ../scripts/run_gen_gds.sh
    ../scripts/run_fill_gds.sh

Copy the hash results from the last of the scripts into doc/hashes.txt

Run LVS and DRC:

    cd validate
    ./run_lvs.sh
    ./run_drc.sh

Run the complete precheck.  The precheck repository can be cloned and
is https://github.com/wafer-space/gf180mcu-precheck

    1. Start a nix-shell with the "shell.nix" file in the repository above.
	e.g.,

	cd ~/gits/gf180mcu-precheck
	nix-shell shell.nix

    2. Run the command:

	python3 precheck.py \
		--input ~/gits/gf180mcu_ocd_sram_test/gf180mcu_ocd_sram2_filled.gds.gz \
		--top gf180mcu_ocd_sram2_top \
		--slot 1x0p5 --cob \
		--workers max --threads 1

Push back to the repository once validated.

-----------------------------------------------------------------
Wafer.Space COB:

Using the breakout board found at:  https://codeberg.org/rebelmike/ws-breakout

This breakout board routes the 70-pin mezzanine connector to two 0.1" row
headers with 35 positions per row.

