Test results below are for the original test chip manufactured on the first
Wafer.Space shuttle run, but the test setup below should be valid for both
versions of the SRAM test chip.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test with single Digilent Analog Discovery 2:
Exercise Lowest four data bits on D and Q, and lowest six address bits.
Start with the 256 byte side.

Assignments:
Digilent signal board pin
-------------------------
DIO 0	 clk	 8

DIO 1	 gwen	 6

DIO 2	 A0	67
DIO 3	 A1	68
DIO 4	 A2	69
DIO 5	 A3	70
DIO 6	 A4	 1
DIO 7	 A5	 2

DIO 8	 Q3/2	27
DIO 9	 Q2/2	26
DIO 10	 Q1/2	23
DIO 11	 Q0/2	22

DIO 12	 D3	60
DIO 13	 D2	59
DIO 14	 D1	58
DIO 15	 D0	57

All Q pins are for the 256 byte macros.
Data and address pins are shared by both sides.

Constant values:
GND	 D4	63
GND	 D5	64
GND	 D6	65
GND	 D7	66

GND	 A6	 3
GND	 A7	 4
GND	 A8	12
GND	 A9	14

GND	 WEN7	40
GND	 WEN6	41
GND	 WEN5	42
GND	 WEN4	43
GND	 WEN3	47
GND	 WEN2	48
GND	 WEN1	49
GND	 WEN0	50

open	 Q4/2	28
open	 Q5/2	29
open	 Q6/2	30
open	 Q7/2	31

GND	 SEL2	13	(select 256 byte bank 1 or 2 on Q/2 outputs)
GND	 SEL5	15	(select 512 or 1024 byte bank on Q/5 outputs))

GND	 CEN1/5	56	(enable all four for starters)
GND	 CEN2/5	55
GND	 CEN1/2	52
GND	 CEN2/2 51

Because the Digilent DIO channels only go to 3.3V, use 3.3V on the
periphery as well as the core (can also test the core at 1.8V).

Local WEN bits are set to zero;  GWEN controls the read/write state.

SEL lines:  GND selects bank 1, VDD selects bank 2

Functional note:  CEN must be high on power-on and then set to zero for
first use.

Writes must be done by setting GWEN low and applying a pulse on CLK, then
returning GWEN high.  The written value is not immediately available at
the output;  reading the output requires an additional pulse on CLK with
GWEN set high.

Additional testing to be done with two Digilent Analog Discovery units
(TBD).  The driver code for testing will be committed to the repository
when it is available.
